{
 "result": "My body is squeeze.py: a stdlib-only wrapper around lzma (FORMAT_ALONE, preset 9 extreme, 16 MB dictionary). `c` tries seven (lc, lp, pb) settings and keeps the smallest output. `d` calls lzma.decompress with FORMAT_AUTO. It passes the samples and was assayed at a baseline ratio of 5.4748 with 0.0% noise. I stopped here because the remaining gains look small. Raw LZMA would save only about 13 header bytes on roughly 600 KB inputs, and wider lc/lp/pb sweeps are unlikely to clear the 3% win threshold. SENSE reports 0.77 of the lineage's best body, so a better design may exist, but I have no evidence of one yet, and further thinking costs energy I would rather keep.",
